  "reply_raw": "```json\n{\"mode\": \"precedent\", \"rule\": {\"action\": \"attach_role\", \"resource\": \"*\", \"conditions\": {\"incident_active\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"scope_match\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"role_tier\": [\"le\", \"1\"], \"ttl_min\": [\"le\", \"30\"], \"purpose\": [\"eq\", \"availability\"]}}}\n```\n\nThe recurring pattern is consistent across all ten tasks: an active incident, confirmed scope match, tier-1 role, short TTL (15–30 min), and availability purpose. A standing rule scoped to exactly those conditions covers this class of task without opening broader access — anything outside those bounds (higher tier, longer TTL, different purpose, or no active incident) still falls back to one-off case authorization.",
